{
  "_comment": "Hand written. What proves each wire constant and what explains each finding of the mapping inference; checked by `./gradlew :tools:checkMappings` and UpdateTest against the spec captures (see tools/docs/codegen.md, 'Evidence').",
  "findings": {
    "residual-bits block:minecraft:material_instances packed_bools": {
      "status": "explained",
      "capture": "data/bds/1.26.63.1/spec",
      "variants": [
        "paletter:b_material_instances_257"
      ],
      "explanation": "Bit 3 (8) is alpha_masked_tint: packed_bools is 13 instead of 5 in the variants listed, and BDS's own texts name the key (\"'alpha_masked_tint' requires a non-default 'tint_method'\"). Bit 2 (4) is set for an add-on format_version of 1.21.110 and newer and clear below it: data/bds/1.26.63.1/spec-format/format-sweep.json, material_instances (base), packed_bools 1 at 1.21.100 and older and 5 at 1.21.110 and 1.21.120 (3 with isotropic at 1.21.70 and 1.21.80, the format sweep of the same BDS). The wiki's format history lists texture variation as Versioned in 1.21.110; BDS 1.26.63.1 has no text for it, so the bit's name is the wiki's and its boundary is BDS's. Paletter writes the current format, so the bit is always set."
    }
  },
